codex
The state model is now fixed: `preparing → prepared → committing → cleanup`, with `rolling_back → rollback_cleanup` on failure. Each target persists `pending → backed_up → committed`; rollback handles crashes that occur between a rename and its state write by inspecting deterministic sibling paths and hashes. Cleanup is itself journaled, so backups are never discarded until every consumer target is durable.
